{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-20145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(2,1,2)$, $B(3,3,3)$, $C(-2,-1,3)$, and $D(4,1,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-20145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i-j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(4i+j+4k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)-2((-4)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)+((-4)\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-4+20+4 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|20|=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-20145" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d67fe3e6f61b1cf14d80c1722873bb5ae7c417577244f6ffc69393aebb4f2b"} {"question" "q-20145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-20145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "20"] ["math" "23"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "29"] ["math" "\\frac{21}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-20145" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "20"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-73736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨t,1,t⟩$, $q=⟨2,-1,-1⟩$, and $r=⟨3,0,1⟩$ are coplanar." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-73736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}t & 1 & t \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+t\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-1))-(2\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-1))+t(2\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =-t-5+3t \\\\  & =2t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 2t-5 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =5 \\\\ t & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=\\frac{5}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-73736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d67fe3e6f61b1cf14d80c1722873bb5ae7c417577244f6ffc69393aebb4f2b"} {"question" "q-73736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-73736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-73736" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,-3,2),$ $B(4,-1,5),$ $C(-2,0,1),$ and $D(3,-2,3).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i-j+5k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j+3k)-(i-3j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(3\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 1)-2((-3)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-3)\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =3(3+1)-2(-3+2)+3(-3-6) \\\\  & =12+2-27 \\\\  & =-13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-13|=13.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d67fe3e6f61b1cf14d80c1722873bb5ae7c417577244f6ffc69393aebb4f2b"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280321" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨4,{k}^{2},2⟩$, $b=⟨1,5,3⟩$, and $c=⟨2,1,0⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n**In ascending order:** $\\,$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}\n$\\,$\nand\n$\\,$\n$k=${{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & {k}^{2} & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-{k}^{2}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 1)-{k}^{2}(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 2)+2(1\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =4(-3)-{k}^{2}(0-6)+2(1-10) \\\\  & =-12+6{k}^{2}-18 \\\\  & =6{k}^{2}-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the triple product equal to 0:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{k}^{2}-30 & =0 \\\\ 6{k}^{2} & =30 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =5 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if \n$k=-\\sqrt{5}$ or $k=\\sqrt{5}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d67fe3e6f61b1cf14d80c1722873bb5ae7c417577244f6ffc69393aebb4f2b"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-280735" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-281023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,0,2),$ $B(3,4,5),$ $C(6,2,4),$ and $D(5,3,6).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-281023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+4j+5k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,4,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(6i+2j+4k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =5i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨5,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(5i+3j+6k)-(i+2k) \\\\  & =4i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨4,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 3)-4(5\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 4)+3(5\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2(8-6)-4(20-8)+3(15-8) \\\\  & =4-48+21 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-23|=23.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-281023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04d67fe3e6f61b1cf14d80c1722873bb5ae7c417577244f6ffc69393aebb4f2b"} {"question" "q-281023" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"} {"question" "q-281023" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "23"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14051998/state.json" "file_sha256" "b8aba0404674312e3cecf18e2ddb1fde29835d579410d6cecc154f445167abaf"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1755 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
